# Sources

`template-dlab5-cloud` is **GPL-3.0-or-later**. See `LICENSE` for the terms and
`COPYRIGHT` for the statement that goes with them.

It was MIT until 2026-08-30. The change is deliberate and, for a template,
consequential: **anything forked from this inherits GPL-3.0**. A project built
on it must be free software too. That is the intent — if a particular piece of
work needs a permissive licence, this is not its starting point.

There were no outside contributors and no forks when the change was made, so
nothing was relicensed on anyone else's behalf. Note that a licence change
cannot reach backwards: anyone who received an earlier version under MIT keeps
those rights for that version.

## Included

Nothing third-party is vendored into this repository.

## Dependencies

All production dependencies are under licences compatible with GPL-3.0: MIT,
ISC, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, MPL-2.0, 0BSD, CC-BY-4.0 and
CC0-1.0. Checked before the relicence with the compatibility scan in
`blueprinting-dlab5-net` (`npm run check:gpl`).

Four packages declare no SPDX identifier and were read by hand: `busboy` and
`streamsearch` (MIT, Brian White), `linkfs` (public domain), and
`xmlhttprequest-ssl` (MIT). None is GPL-incompatible.
